<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-ad0fbd869a064b728810a45136f496ce" title="sat-c2-u07-affluent.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>D</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;affluent&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">The orchard enjoyed an affluent pear harvest this fall, with crates of fruit stacked clear to the rafters of the barn.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">His affluent closing argument moved fully half the jury to tears before the judge had even finished charging them.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">By June the snowmelt turns the creek affluent, doubling its speed beneath the old footbridge.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">Advertisers pay a premium to reach the magazine&apos;s affluent readers, who renovate kitchens and vacation abroad.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Affluent means wealthy, with money flowing in beyond need, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a big pear harvest is an abundance of fruit, not of money — plentiful is not the same claim as affluent.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Affluent means wealthy, with money flowing in beyond need, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a speech can be fluent or eloquent — words flowing well — but affluence is about wealth, not delivery.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Affluent means wealthy, with money flowing in beyond need, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because the creek&apos;s current is literal water; the flowing inside affluent is a fossil metaphor about money, never an actual stream.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Affluent means wealthy, with money flowing in beyond need, so it&apos;s the correct answer because readers who renovate kitchens and vacation abroad are exactly the money-to-spare audience advertisers pay extra to reach.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
